@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

libdtfl is a C11 library for data-parallel dataflow computation.  It is
a port of three Rust projects: @emph{timely dataflow}, a runtime for
cyclic dataflows with partially ordered timestamps and progress
tracking; @emph{differential dataflow}, incrementally maintained
collections built on it; and the @emph{timely diagnostics} tools.  A
program builds a dataflow graph of operators, feeds it data at logical
timestamps, and reads results back as the computation makes progress.
Differential dataflow adds collections whose contents are maintained
incrementally: change an input and only the affected outputs are
recomputed.

Include @file{dtfl/dtfl.h} and link with @option{-ldtfl}, or use
@command{pkg-config --cflags --libs dtfl}.  The reference pages for every
function are in manual sections 1, 3 and 7; see @ref{API Reference}.
This manual is the tutorial and conceptual companion to those pages: it
teaches the model and walks through worked examples, all in C against
the actual libdtfl API.

